/**
 * =========================================================================
 * RASPBERRY PI REACT DEPLOYMENT BLUEPRINT
 * =========================================================================
 * 
 * Your portfolio website is built using React ("my-react-app"). Because 
 * React uses a JSX compilation layer, updating the source files or running 
 * a standard "git pull" alone will not show changes on your live site. 
 * 
 * Every time you push a frontend modification from your local computer, 
 * you must compile the application into static production assets on the Pi 
 * and move them into the Nginx/Apache web root directory (/var/www/html/).
 * 
 * -------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * LIVE UPDATING PROCEDURE (Run these via your SSH terminal window)
 * -------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * 
 * STEP 1: Log back into your Raspberry Pi via PowerShell or Terminal:
 * ssh grayson@raspberrypi.local
 * 
 * STEP 2: Navigate directly into your repository source tracking workspace:
 * cd ~/Portfolio
 * 
 * STEP 3: Grab your latest codebase modifications from GitHub:
 * git pull
 * 
 * STEP 4: Navigate directly into your core React ecosystem folder:
 * cd my-react-app
 * 
 * STEP 5: Compile your updated JSX layout & assets into production bundles:
 * npm run build
 * 
 * STEP 6: Safely remove any stale, cached site files from your web hosting root:
 * sudo rm -rf /var/www/html/*
 * 
 * STEP 7: Copy your newly compiled production build into the live server directory:
 * sudo cp -r dist/* /var/www/html/
 * 
 * STEP 8: Reload your core web server daemon to instantly pipe out changes:
 * sudo systemctl restart nginx || sudo systemctl restart apache2
 * 
 * STEP 9: Force your browser to drop stale history and render the new layout:
 * Press "Ctrl + F5" (Windows) or "Cmd + Shift + R" (Mac) on the portfolio URL.
 * 
 * =========================================================================
 */
